      "question": "How do foreign central banks justify their recent decision to lower interest rates, and what specific economic indicators are they monitoring to guide these policy shifts?",
      "quote": "Many foreign central banks, including the European Central Bank and the Bank of Canada as well as several central banks in Latin America and Southeast Asia, continued to cut policy rates since mid-2024, citing declining inflationary pressures, easing labor markets, and concerns about economic growth. Policymakers generally emphasized that they are following a data-dependent",
